<!-- Read-only query user for the Sigma runner (full example gaps).

ClickHouse loads this fragment because it is a file in the users config directory:
  "The directory users.d is used by default, as users_config defaults to users.xml. User
   configuration fragments are merged in lexicographical order by their full paths."
  https://clickhouse.com/docs/concepts/features/configuration/server-config/configuration-files
  (read 2026-09-08; the pinned image is clickhouse/clickhouse-server:25.12.5 per
   components/data/store-signoz/versions.json, and this store already relies on users.d by
   mounting clickhouse-query-mem.xml at /etc/clickhouse-server/users.d/query-mem.xml).

What the user may NOT do, and which setting enforces it:
  readonly = 1      "Only read data queries are allowed" plus "the user can't change readonly and
                    allow_ddl settings in the current session"
                    (docs/concepts/features/configuration/settings/permissions-for-queries).
                    An INSERT, OPTIMIZE, CREATE, ALTER, DROP or TRUNCATE is refused.
  allow_ddl = 0     The docs list allow_ddl separately from readonly with default 1, so readonly
                    alone would still permit DDL. Both are set.
  grants            SELECT on the three SigNoz signal databases only. Everything else, including
                    system tables and any other database, is unreachable: "GRANT SELECT ON db.*
                    ... allows john to execute the SELECT query over all the tables in db database"
                    (docs/reference/statements/grant).

The password is NOT in this file. It is substituted at config load from the file named by
include_from, which is ClickHouse's documented way to keep a value out of a shipped config:
  "If an element has the attribute incl, its value will be replaced by the content of the
   referenced file. The path to the file with substitutions is set by the include_from element in
   the server config ... The substitution values are specified in /clickhouse/substitution_name
   elements in this file. If a substitution specified in incl does not exist, it is recorded in
   the log."
   Same page, section "Substitution with file content". Note that page's caveat: include_from is
   read per configuration file, and the users config is loaded separately from the server config,
   so include_from belongs HERE, in a users.d fragment, not in config.d.

That missing-substitution sentence is the reason the credential is a REQUIRED Compose secret in
the sibling compose.yaml and never a default: an unresolvable incl leaves
the element empty, which in ClickHouse means a user with no password. Compose refuses to render
when a required secret's file does not exist, so the failure happens at `config` time, in front of
the operator, instead of as a silent anonymous read account on the project network.

settings and constraints: the runner posts max_execution_time, max_rows_to_read,
max_bytes_to_read, max_memory_usage, max_result_rows, result_overflow_mode, read_overflow_mode and
query parameters (param_start_ns, param_end_ns, param_resource_id, param_dataset) with every query
(local_observe/platform/sigma_runner.py, ClickHouse.query). Under readonly = 1 "settings cannot be
changed unless changeable_in_readonly is set"
(docs/concepts/features/configuration/settings/constraints-on-settings), so each of those bounds is
declared here AND marked changeable_in_readonly: the profile is what binds the user, so the value
holds even if a client sends nothing, and the exception exists only so the runner's own request is
not refused. Nothing else may be changed by this user.

Status: reviewed shape, never executed. There was no Docker host where full example gaps was drafted, and
components/control/sigma/conformance.md still lists "dedicated HTTP query-user permissions" as an
open gate. examples/full/README.md states the three commands that prove this file does what it
claims before anything depends on it.
-->
<clickhouse>
    <include_from>/run/secrets/clickhouse-query-credentials</include_from>
    <profiles>
        <lo-readonly>
            <readonly>1</readonly>
            <allow_ddl>0</allow_ddl>
            <!-- The same bounds the runner asks for, held server side. max_memory_usage here is a
                 tenth of the 1 GiB the store's default profile allows a query (query-mem.xml), so
                 a runaway Sigma window costs this user less memory than it costs SigNoz's own UI
                 queries. -->
            <max_execution_time>5</max_execution_time>
            <max_rows_to_read>1000000</max_rows_to_read>
            <max_bytes_to_read>67108864</max_bytes_to_read>
            <max_memory_usage>134217728</max_memory_usage>
            <max_result_rows>1</max_result_rows>
            <result_overflow_mode>throw</result_overflow_mode>
            <read_overflow_mode>throw</read_overflow_mode>
            <constraints>
                <max_execution_time><changeable_in_readonly/></max_execution_time>
                <max_rows_to_read><changeable_in_readonly/></max_rows_to_read>
                <max_bytes_to_read><changeable_in_readonly/></max_bytes_to_read>
                <max_memory_usage><changeable_in_readonly/></max_memory_usage>
                <max_result_rows><changeable_in_readonly/></max_result_rows>
                <result_overflow_mode><changeable_in_readonly/></result_overflow_mode>
                <read_overflow_mode><changeable_in_readonly/></read_overflow_mode>
            </constraints>
        </lo-readonly>
    </profiles>
    <users>
        <lo-query>
            <!-- Resolved from /clickhouse/lo_query_password inside the include_from file. The file
                 holds the same value as LO_CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD_FILE, which the runner presents as
                 its key, so ClickHouse must know it in the same form: a <password> element is the
                 plaintext method, which is what an X-ClickHouse-Key header over the project network
                 authenticates against. -->
            <password incl="lo_query_password"/>
            <profile>lo-readonly</profile>
            <quota>default</quota>
            <!-- No address restriction: the runner is a container on the Compose network whose
                 address is not stable, and the store's own boundary is that network plus this
                 password. Narrow these two entries to your project subnet if you can name it. -->
            <networks>
                <ip>0.0.0.0/0</ip>
                <ip>::/0</ip>
            </networks>
            <grants>
                <grant>GRANT SELECT ON signoz_traces.*</grant>
                <grant>GRANT SELECT ON signoz_metrics.*</grant>
                <grant>GRANT SELECT ON signoz_logs.*</grant>
            </grants>
        </lo-query>
    </users>
</clickhouse>
